    {
      "id": "03-fats",
      "index": 2,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "fats",
      "text": "60.8 grams of fat. Saturated fat is 4.5 grams, which is reasonably controlled for a high-fat nut. Omega 3 is 90 milligrams, so it is not doing much for omega 3 support. Polyunsaturated fat is 7.9 grams, another weaker fat-quality mark. For nuts, the fat section matters because most of the calories are coming from fat.",
      "textSha256": "58a3ea31bb878a89ce202a8411d344dffa5169805c7dcc727bbc78eda995625a",
      "characterCount": 319,
      "byteLength": 340680,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/hazelnuts/voice-v1-blocks/03-fats.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "UMgLkwY88Zu3T7ycWpQI",
        "historyItemId": "HDAkw8DMA9o9QzDp45d0"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/hazelnuts/voice/voice-v1-blocks/03-fats.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-carbs",
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "carbs",
      "text": "16.7 grams of carbs. Glycemic index is 15, helping the carbs behave steadily. Fibre is 9.7 grams, which is a useful fullness and digestion mark. Starch is 0 grams, so this is not really a steady-starch fuel. For nuts, carbs are not the main job, but fibre and sugar still decide whether the snack feels balanced.",
      "textSha256": "d37564bdf9537375437e69360bb07db1a54bf23f6f84c61655e539739ee2353c",
      "characterCount": 312,
      "byteLength": 351129,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/hazelnuts/voice-v1-blocks/04-carbs.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "PTKJwhG9lZZ1DkWG6yKf",
        "historyItemId": "5hqHUDGJCcA3NY7MiHeu"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/hazelnuts/voice/voice-v1-blocks/04-carbs.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-proteins",
      "index": 4,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "proteins",
      "text": "15 grams of protein. That amount is useful enough to count. Essential amino acids score is 5 out of 9, so the quality is okay but not strong enough to make this a main protein source. For nuts, protein helps, but it is still a supporting role.",
      "textSha256": "d7b1755605f3db94ef6ae13473a722ddd4a6bc02f9a2eddb97f11219dc75ab97",
      "characterCount": 243,
      "byteLength": 238698,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/hazelnuts/voice-v1-blocks/05-proteins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "YwPWoF1UQxSaAPYSJr8o",
        "historyItemId": "GzsDY4ui3P81E4eo7jdY"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/hazelnuts/voice/voice-v1-blocks/05-proteins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-vitamins",
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "vitamins",
      "text": "Vitamin E is 100% daily value, a huge strength for antioxidant support. For nuts, vitamin E can be the micronutrient that makes the high-fat package look much more useful.",
      "textSha256": "d2bc823f201c2f036c98a71cc6ed9023a0b65ea8c4b4dfcde2be41304dfcb918",
      "characterCount": 171,
      "byteLength": 168899,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/hazelnuts/voice-v1-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "JWqZiscM50B3tw7oP4fj",
        "historyItemId": "QlMJMNTCLtpA0Xs9Drfi"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/hazelnuts/voice/voice-v1-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-minerals",
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "minerals",
      "text": "Magnesium is 41% daily value, the best mineral here and useful for muscle, nerve, and energy-metabolism support. Iron is 26% daily value, a decent blood-and-oxygen mark. Zinc is 18% daily value, present but not strong enough to make immune support a headline. For nuts, minerals help justify the dense calorie package, and hazelnuts are good but not elite here.",
      "textSha256": "e7adb41bc4177c277adcb12bb3e428ea5d808facd07c145b97b7fc1a6647a7a7",
      "characterCount": 361,
      "byteLength": 381640,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/hazelnuts/voice-v1-blocks/07-minerals.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "ffzenVQRp9Hx4Nh3pEs0",
        "historyItemId": "wn6U8ywWvCLW6B7EUSfu"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/hazelnuts/voice/voice-v1-blocks/07-minerals.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-pros",
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "pros",
      "text": "Positives first: still a recognisable whole-food option. That keeps them cleaner than most processed snacks. Holds up as a better snack default than most packaged options. That real-world swap value counts. Fat and texture help satiety. They can hold up better than many snack foods.",
      "textSha256": "ff5882721ad4163653dc260318465491df7c4c3ebbf4eb0f149e38f7a5441ff0",
      "characterCount": 283,
      "byteLength": 275061,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/hazelnuts/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "WkaDr5A86XGwL9T27RLj",
        "historyItemId": "6XwtbZAuAVLrN9hckxik"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/hazelnuts/voice/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "Cons next: needs the right supporting foods. It works better as part of a fuller plate than as the whole answer. Good versions can get expensive. That affects how realistic frequent use is. Portion control can get slippery fast. Dense foods punish casual handful math.",
      "textSha256": "6fd9144bd2b3c15acfc53ad692cc3361d763dde473a9a1112a38ab8b54922978",
      "characterCount": 268,
      "byteLength": 268373,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/hazelnuts/voice-v1-blocks/09-cons.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "jVKg9wgmiAlsxuuqcXr4",
        "historyItemId": "NeLGFBEbQJj8PGK1im3x"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/hazelnuts/voice/voice-v1-blocks/09-cons.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-closing_summary",
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "closing_summary",
      "sectionKey": null,
      "text": "Best bits are vitamin E, steady carb behaviour, and the snack role. Weak spots are omega 3, zinc, and portion control. Best for better snack swaps, satiety, and vitamin E support because the texture is satisfying and the carb section stays pretty controlled.",
      "textSha256": "8e3f581e6c96948d14896bd170b7d50aa46c72dd712b157454421106c4ebeb1a",
      "characterCount": 258,
